-- title:
--   Integrality of the k-fibre of the two-chart model
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ be a natural number and let $k$ be a field in which the image of $N$ is a unit. Write $F_N$ for the intermediate field `modularFunctionFieldFull N` of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$, namely the subfield generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,j_q$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$, and let $j =$ `jFull N` be the element of $F_N$ given by the $q$-expansion $j_q$ itself. Let $\mathfrak{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel ℤ F_N j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the scheme obtained by gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $F_N$ generated by $j$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$ along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the subalgebra generated by both (the pushout of the two affine morphisms `fFin` and `fInf`), and let `toBase` be the morphism $\mathfrak{X} \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$ assembled from the structure morphisms of the two charts. The assertion is that the fibre product of `toBase` with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring map $\mathbb{Z} \to k$, that is the scheme $\mathfrak{X}\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}}\operatorname{Spec}k$, is an integral scheme: nonempty, irreducible and reduced.
--
--   This is the statement that the model of the modular curve attached to the field of modular functions of level $N$ has integral fibres over all fields of residue characteristic not dividing $N$ (good reduction away from $N$, in the classical form going back to Igusa and to Deligne–Rapoport). It is used downstream for the integrality, local Noetherianity and stalk statements about the Deligne–Rapoport level structures and about the Igusa scheme.
